{
  "id": "arith-002",
  "title": "Average of three readings",
  "concept": "arithmetic",
  "difficulty": 1,
  "prompt": "The robot's sensor takes three readings. Find their average, keeping the decimals. average_of_three(1, 1, 2) is 1.333…",
  "signature": "func average_of_three(a, b, c) -> float:",
  "fn": "average_of_three",
  "starter": "func average_of_three(a, b, c) -> float:\n\treturn 0.0",
  "tests": [
    {
      "name": "1, 2, 3 average 2",
      "args": [
        1,
        2,
        3
      ],
      "expect": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "10, 20, 30 average 20",
      "args": [
        10,
        20,
        30
      ],
      "expect": 20
    },
    {
      "name": "1, 1, 2 keeps decimals",
      "args": [
        1,
        1,
        2
      ],
      "expect": 1.3333333333
    },
    {
      "name": "All zero is 0",
      "args": [
        0,
        0,
        0
      ],
      "expect": 0
    },
    {
      "name": "2, 3, 4 average 3",
      "args": [
        2,
        3,
        4
      ],
      "expect": 3
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Add a, b and c in brackets first, then divide the whole sum by three.",
    "Dividing by 3 (an int) loses the decimals; divide by 3.0.",
    "`return (a + b + c) / 3.0`"
  ],
  "docs": [],
  "solution": "func average_of_three(a, b, c) -> float:\n\treturn (a + b + c) / 3.0",
